obs FOUR renumbers, not three: %439 -> %440 -> %444 -> %446, one per fetch, and the send's commit body froze at the third because the final amend carried the message forward with -C HEAD while the files had moved on. Pushed before I read it back. The body is testimony now, so an erratum sits in the row itself -- and the stamp 20260905.230021 identifies the row through all four numbers, which is exactly what the derived-spine law puts identity in the stamp FOR.
obs The lesson I would hand the next hand: re-read the commit body against the files after a message-preserving amend. -C HEAD keeps a message that was true two rebases ago, and nothing in the wall reads a ledger number against the ledger.
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- two things want your word and neither is mine to take: %446 is fleet friction in bakery's lane with the mechanism already built and one nuance booked, and the 14 of ratchet slack is a one-line tightening that changes a fleet-wide gate. Next kg in my own lane is bron-resins/, the other half of this seat.
